# Director - the 2D-view click routes.
#
# The stage PAGE now lives in rundown.mast: picking a subject and choosing a shot turned out to
# be one job, not two, so Stage and Camera merged into one editor. What is left here is the
# part that was never a page - the routes that turn a click on the 2D view into a subject.
#
# The console these fire for is named `gamemaster_director_sci`, set by the editor:
#   * `gamemaster_` prefix -> the engine optimized network path for detached command consoles.
#   * `sci` in the name    -> consoledispatcher routes a 2D-view click to the SCIENCE
#                             selection, which is what //focus/science below reads. A name
#                             matching none of its substrings falls through to
#                             normal_target_UID and the clicks drive nothing at all.

# The rundown the editor is adding to. Set on the editor page; read by its actions.
default shared cv_target_rundown = None

# Selection handling, adapted from the Game Master (gamemaster.mast //focus/science).
#
# TWO WAYS IN, one route. A click on the 2D view and a row picked off the science object list
# both convert to `science_target_UID` (consoledispatcher.convert), so both land here - which
# is why the Stage tab can offer the list beside the radar and have it stage the same subject.
#
# extra_extra_tag carries lmb/rmb; blank is a fake event. Left-click on empty space PANS the
# camera to that point; picking an object - from either surface - pans to it AND makes it the
# subject. Right is left alone, matching the GM, so a right-drag stays available to the engine.
#
# The route runs SERVER-side, so `shared` is on the write - a bare assignment would bind a
# task-local and the shot tab would go on reading the old subject forever.
//focus/science if has_roles(SCIENCE_ORIGIN_ID, "director_cam")
    # The origin can be gone - the cam is a real object and a GM area-delete brush can take
    # it. Without this the whole route raises on a dead reference.
    ->END if SCIENCE_ORIGIN is None
    # Right is left alone, matching the GM, so a right-drag stays available to the engine.
    ->END if EVENT.extra_extra_tag == "rmb"
    # SELECTION FIRST, source_point only if there is no selection - and that order is what
    # makes the science object list usable at all. A list row carries a selection but not
    # necessarily a clicked POINT, and `Vec3(None)` raises AttributeError - which stops the
    # MAST command, ends the route, and leaves picking from the list doing nothing at all with
    # nothing logged. Reading the point first put that raise ahead of every other line here.
    if SCIENCE_SELECTED_ID != 0 and SCIENCE_SELECTED is not None:
        shared cv_subject_id = SCIENCE_SELECTED_ID
        # STAGE IT HERE, not from the editor's `on change`. The bench is what every Preview
        # screen follows, and pushing it at the point the subject is actually picked means the
        # preview updates on the click rather than on the next repaint.
        director_stage_subject(SCIENCE_SELECTED_ID)
        cv_focus_pos = Vec3(SCIENCE_SELECTED.pos)
    elif EVENT.source_point is not None:
        cv_focus_pos = Vec3(EVENT.source_point)
    else:
        ->END
    # KEEP THE HEIGHT. The cam spawns above the plane so the 2D view reads like a plan;
    # copying the target position wholesale drops it to the target own altitude on the first
    # click and it never comes back up. The GM and the OU Admiral both do that and both are
    # worse for it.
    cv_focus_pos.y = SCIENCE_ORIGIN.pos.y
    SCIENCE_ORIGIN.pos = cv_focus_pos

# Scan data is stored per the ORIGIN SIDE, so one pass marks a whole side objects known and
# comms/science enable on the first click rather than the second.
#
# science_update_scan_data, NOT science_set_scan_data with a bare string: the bare-string form
# builds an empty tab list and then writes it, clobbering the target scan_type_list to ""
# for every ship on the side. The update form merges instead.
//enable/science if has_roles(SCIENCE_ORIGIN_ID, "director_cam")
    science_update_scan_data(SCIENCE_ORIGIN_ID, SCIENCE_SELECTED_ID, "Director")

# Keep every director cam seeing new arrivals. The link is made once at spawn against the
# ships that existed THEN, so without this a contact that arrives later is invisible to the
# stage view - the same reason the GM carries this route.
//spawn if has_any_role(SPAWNED_ID, "ship,station")
    for _dc in role("director_cam"):
        link(_dc, "extra_scan_source", to_set(SPAWNED_ID))
